}^{7}{b}^{2}-12{a}^{5}-8{a}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481373 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f5e6d20-6d83-5a4b-9919-511354ddc37f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-87" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480828} {:answer/id #uuid "76d69649-f0c6-5771-848d-71954873581b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "87" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480957} {:answer/id #uuid "b381b4b1-c1bc-52ab-8b7e-21ef5860d874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-89" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481079} {:answer/id #uuid "e6602306-1f53-57b5-91c7-8b39e35659a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "89" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481178} {:answer/id #uuid "fdeff659-436b-5f34-ac81-a6409e40fce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-121" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f5e6d20-6d83-5a4b-9919-511354ddc37f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-87" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480828} :answer-field/id #uuid "93d546fe-e93e-5d3c-8f24-4f640019211e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481291}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5e5e796d-b724-597d-a614-e8af03095fdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-100301" :question/problem "Calculate ${(\\frac{8}{7}-\\frac{1}{16})}^{0}-11\\times {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-3}.$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, notice that\n$\\frac{8}{7}-\\frac{1}{16}$\nis not zero. Any non-zero number raised to the power of $0$ equals $1.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n{(\\frac{8}{7}-\\frac{1}{16})}^{0}=1.\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the negative exponent and get\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-3}={(\\frac{2}{1})}^{3}={2}^{3}=8.\n$$\n\nSubstituting all these values into the expression, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{8}{7}-\\frac{1}{16})}^{0}-11\\times {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-3} & = \\\\ 1-11\\times 8 & = \\\\ 1-88 & = \\\\ -87\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481375 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff108b6d-b341-5dec-bcea-441b760861b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff108b6d-b341-5dec-bcea-441b760861b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481234} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bea4dc1-0a50-536e-8358-41147aeb0b3f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481263}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6433a3cf-883a-54aa-9f03-bdc753346e58" :question/math-academy-id "q-175958" :question/problem "$\\frac{5}{36}\\times 2+(5+1)^{-2}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, we compute the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{36}\\times 2+(5+1)^{-2}=\\frac{5}{36}\\times 2+{6}^{-2}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that ${6}^{-2}=\\frac{1}{{6}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{36}.$ So, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{36}\\times 2+{6}^{-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{36}\\times 2+\\frac{1}{36} & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{36}\\times \\frac{2}{1}+\\frac{1}{36} & = \\\\ \\frac{5\\times 2}{36\\times 1}+\\frac{1}{36} & = \\\\ \\frac{10}{36}+\\frac{1}{36} & = \\\\ \\frac{10+1}{36} & = \\\\ \\frac{11}{36}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-fiel