 the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}÷(1-{3}^{2}) & = \\\\ \\sqrt{5}÷(1-9) & = \\\\ \\sqrt{5}÷(-8) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{(-8)} & = \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482519 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ceeec55a-62de-5adb-8c13-58418f561ead" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ceeec55a-62de-5adb-8c13-58418f561ead" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482265} :answer-field/id #uuid "04f7fdd5-6526-50c1-bd2d-3e03d282d11e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482381} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43231816-88c3-5bce-9682-f610fb3f3fd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43231816-88c3-5bce-9682-f610fb3f3fd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481938} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0a2a356-681d-59da-b7f5-816fe79f7dc4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2d137423-8c38-5c63-aa2d-733719761261" :question/math-academy-id "q-216488" :question/problem "${(2{x}^{2}+3)}^{2}\\,\\,=\\,\\,${{field-1}}${x}^{4}\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,\\,+9$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the following formula:\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{2}={a}^{2}+2ab+{b}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=2{x}^{2}$ and $b=3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(2{x}^{2}+3)}^{2} & = \\\\ {(2{x}^{2})}^{2}+2(2{x}^{2})(3)+{3}^{2} & = \\\\ 4{x}^{4}+12{x}^{2}+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482533 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2745bb24-5840-55f6-931d-2b152d735984" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481876} {:answer/id #uuid "a5a8a3c9-56b8-5913-910e-d95965c0e447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482168} {:answer/id #uuid "d3720577-5e59-5eea-84ee-913448cf58d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482280} {:answer/id #uuid "d51ebc77-78d2-534b-b4fc-e2f01d991b1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482285} {:answer/id #uuid "dd8d183a-6251-5c2b-b30e-a4b52550966d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3720577-5e59-5eea-84ee-913448cf58d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482280} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a879489-ac5d-5d24-945a-940805770edd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "442c94f9-fe8b-546a-8c5a-f7942d124959" :question/math-academy-id "q-69121" :question/problem "$(-2)\\times (4.1-\\sqrt{4})=$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)\\times (4.1-\\sqrt{4}) & = \\\\ (-2)\\times (4.1-\\sqrt{2\\cdot 2}) & = \\\\ (-2)\\times (4.1-\\sqrt{{2}^{2}}) & = \\\\ (-2)\\times (4.1-2) & = \\\\ (-2)\\times (2.1) & = \\\\ -4.2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482537 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c288773-6605-52e2-ac4b-f6bd250f6881" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.643" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481849} {:answer/id #uuid "4350ad3f-e88d-53a1-8fb1-12f2d61c6199" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.427" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481940} {:answer/id #uuid "4bde511a-ac2b-53f9-9089-b2a6e07cae57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.899" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481956} {:answer/id #uuid "5c2a9045-efd9-5aad-b59b-8f3ff267f05c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481992} {:answer/id #uuid "ab724880-144d-5d22-87ae-cf2b3816162c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.351" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bde511a-ac2b-53f9-9089-b2a6e07cae57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.899" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481956} :answer-field/id #uuid "caa3dfcf-a676-51da-a5bf-f83fd246ee39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482481}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4ae171d6-ef6c-513e-bb69-e2d14e0a590f" :question/math-academy-id "q-69265" :question/problem "What is the value of $2\\sqrt{(3-6)\\times (1-3)}$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?" :question/worked-solution "To simplify the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{(3-6)\\times (1-3)} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{(-3)\\times (-2)} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we approximate the value of the radical using a calculator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & ≈‭‭‭2.449\\,490\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\nFinally, we approximate the value of the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{6} & ≈ \\\\ 2(2.449\\,490) & ≈ \\\\ 4.898\\,98 & ≈ \\\\ 4.899\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482538 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0562085d-1c8a-584a-8b9e-4c5bbb910216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{w}^{2}+12vw+4{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481782} {:answer/id #uuid "841164ba-f898-5db4-97c6-db88d7dfe42b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(3w+2v)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482079} {:answer/id #uuid "ad866c36-d5dd-5dfd-bbb3-8a9e056f52dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{w}^{2}+4{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482183} {:answer/id #uuid "b632ec41-2c3a-5c38-bbbd-12393d29dbfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{w}^{2}+4vw+4{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482207} {:answer/id #uuid "baddd21b-12e1-5ee9-983e-9b4cef19aab4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{w}^{2}+12vw" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482220}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0562085d-1c8a-584a-8b9e-4c5bbb910216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{w}^{2}+12vw+4{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481782} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9264828-72bc-5feb-b279-b58d31b33327" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b635fc4-723b-5734-9d78-9acb6ad51368" :question/math-academy-id "q-111370" :question/problem "${(3w+2v)}^{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the following formula:\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{2}={a}^{2}+2ab+{b}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=3w$ and $b=2v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(3w+2v)}^{2} & = \\\\ {(3w)}^{2}+2(3w)(2v)+{(2v)}^{2} & = \\\\ 9{w}^{2}+12vw+4{v}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482541 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b824ae97-0782-520b-98c2-6828b4f4b7ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.742" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b824ae97-0782-520b-98c2-6828b4f4b7ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.742" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482212} :answer-field/id #uuid "40f14f8c-bc9b-58e2-900b-314d7347ebbd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482414}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "531dca87-ee51-5a1e-9c95-aee21eccb0e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-171401" :question/problem "Rounded to $3$ decimal places, $\\sqrt{6+4\\times 2}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To simplify the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6+4\\times 2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{6+8} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{14}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we approximate the value of $\\sqrt{14}$ using a calculator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{14} & ≈‭‭‭3.742\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482545 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc71a8d3-77ed-5983-91d4-679b83fe7eca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc71a8d3-77ed-5983-91d4-679b83fe7eca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482259} :answer-field/id #uuid "273cdb84-4cc2-5fe9-9f07-531b9b3f30b8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482399} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9f67e05-cb2a-5935-9b20-22131047e3c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9f67e05-cb2a-5935-9b20-22131047e3c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482293} :answer-field/id #uuid "85dccd4b-b234-5244-8261-362adba1349e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482450} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b4f3577-ea48-51d4-9617-02afb3d566b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b4f3577-ea48-51d4-9617-02afb3d566b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "